// lib/warning.synl
//
// Standard library: warning (Synth-OOP interface).
// 标准库：warning（Synth-OOP 接口）。
//
// [EXPERIMENTAL / 实验性] The public shape of this library may change without
// notice before the 1.0 freeze. Pin a commit if you depend on it.
// 本库公开形态在 1.0 冻结前可能未经预告即变更。依赖时请锁定提交。
//
// The behavioral face of the `warning` library; the real work is done by the
// C++ backend in lib/cpp/warning.hpp. Importing `&warning;` registers the
// native class, then interprets this file — the class is already registered,
// so the definition here documents the public shape. Any `$Program` class in a
// library is ignored.
// `warning` 库的行为形态；真实工作由 lib/cpp/warning.hpp 的 C++ 底层完成。
// `&warning;` 导入时登记原生类，再解释本文件——该类已登记，故此定义
// 仅作为公开形态的文档。库中的 `$Program` 类会被忽略。
//
// Method signatures below carry their type constraints; the interpreter
// enforces them at the call boundary. The authoritative enforced signature
// lives in lib/cpp/warning.hpp's make_sign; this file mirrors it.
// 下列方法签名均带类型约束；解释器在调用边界强制检查。强制检查的权威签名
// 位于 lib/cpp/warning.hpp 的 make_sign；本文件是其可读镜像。

$Raise {
    // The constructor emits a non-fatal warning to the standard error stream
    // (prefixed `[WARNING]`) and stores `code` / `message` on the instance so
    // callers can query them afterwards (e.g. `warn.code`, `warn.message`,
    // or `w := warning::Raise(...)`). Execution continues — warnings are
    // treated as specific output, not as fatal conditions.
    // 构造函数向标准错误流输出非致命警告（带 `[WARNING]` 前缀），并把 `code` /
    // `message` 存到实例上，供调用方随后查询（如 `warn.code`、`warn.message`、
    // 或 `w := warning::Raise(...)`）。其后执行继续——警告被视为特定输出，
    // 而非致命状况。
    @::[(code[std::String], message[std::String]) ~> () { }];
    // Queryable fields / 可查询字段：code[std::String], message[std::String]
}
